  "notes": [
    "The dual GPU pool runs one independent DeepSeek runtime per GPU and assigns requests by queue depth.",
    "The layer-pipeline benchmark runs layers 0-12 on GPU0 and layers 13-26 + LM head on GPU1 and produces token-for-token parity with the single-GPU baseline.",
    "The NCCL all-to-all smoke validates real ExpertPacket transport and hot-expert token sharding across both GPUs.",
    "The expert-sharded runtime splits routed expert chunks by ECS owner across GPU0/GPU1; the in-model activation exchange was subsequently moved to NCCL point-to-point between coordinator and remote expert worker.",
    "The asynchronous NCCL revision overlaps remote expert requests with local expert chunks: exact token parity, 4.90 tok/s decode, 2.02 s prefill, and ~39.6 MB peak GPU allocation on the remote rank.",
    "Continuous batching is now implemented: staggered requests enter fixed slots, finished rows are removed, and new prefills append to the live KV cache. Four staggered requests completed correctly with heartbeat healthy; aggregate decode 4.21 tok/s, still below fixed-batch throughput because of per-request prefill and cache reorder overhead."
  ],
